# Live tuning overlay

Focus-driven tree panel: session -> view state -> `RowLayout` -> draw. Overlay Latin text uses bundled DejaVu Sans Mono; icons use Material Icons in `assets/fonts/`.

## Collapsible UI lexicon

- **Expandable section:** header with expand arrow; Left/Right toggles a session-only `expanded` flag; children live in `RowLayout` and are omitted when collapsed.
- **Inspector group:** Settings and Project fields. The header is the sub-group row kind. Open and closed state lives on the shell focus collapsed set, not a session `expanded` flag. A collapsed group hides its children.
- **Conditional rows:** sibling rows shown or hidden by a value predicate; no arrow or expanded flag.
- **Panel anchor:** header looks like an expandable section but content lives in a separate host (timeline strip). Do not fold the timeline strip into `RowLayout`.

`RowLayout` rebuilds only when `view_state_structure_signature()` changes. Conditional rows are included or omitted at build time. A field that gates row presence must be in that signature; omit value-only fields. Add a `test_structure_signature_invalidates_on_*` test in `tests/cleave/viz/test_view_state_structure.py`.

New rows: `RowKind` + `RowSpec` + `SectionNode`. No per-`RowKind` label or mutation branches in `tuning_panel_draw.py` or `controls.py`. Overlay chrome lives in `overlay_primitives`; timeline, help, and modal must not import `tuning_panel_draw`. `render_visibility_icon` stays in `row_present_renderers.py`.

## Parameterized actions

When an action needs parameters, keep the panel row as a plain `ACTION` line. On Enter, chain one modal per parameter, then apply.

Exception: timeline preset parameters live as child value rows under an expandable section; apply confirms with Yes/Cancel and lists staged choices as `labeled_lines`.

## Render `enabled`

`enabled=False` on a render header must skip that block in the frame path, not only dim panel rows. Overlay cards gate per card. Post-FX children must check `session.render_post_fx.enabled`. New post-FX subsections need an `enabled=False` test.

## Typography

Colors live in `cleave/viz/theme.py`. Use existing roles (`LABEL`, `VALUE`, `ACTION`, `DISABLED`, `LOCKED`) plus the accent constants already there. Do not invent a new color without adding a theme constant.

Label+value rows: prefix in `LABEL`, value in the row value color. Expand arrows use the value role. Exceptions (single-color action rows, settings/config headers, transport, notifications, modals) are deliberate; match nearby rows.

## Keyboard dispatch

Layered in `input_dispatch.py`. Modal keys first. Then Tab / Shift+Tab cycles Menu, Navigator, Inspector, and Timeline (Timeline is skipped when the strip is closed; the leftover panel is never a Tab stop). Then the menu bar, command shortcuts, and Ctrl+Up / Ctrl+Down (previous / next top-level navigator node; no effect while the menu bar is focused). Then other globals, then the active region. The navigator and inspector own arrows, Enter, Esc, and PageUp/PageDown. Other keys fall through to the leftover panel. Timeline keys stay on the strip when that region is active. `h` stays global even when the timeline strip has focus.

Settings and Project fields are inspector groups (`SETTINGS_SECTION`, `PROJECT_SECTION`). Layer, render, timeline, and song-marker rows stay on the leftover panel.
